module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ExceptionalCartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.Transform.FittingFlatten
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartierAffineLocal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FittingIdealSheaf.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Fitting.ProjectiveDimension

/-!
# Projective dimension of a module pulled back to the blowup of its Fitting ideal

Let `ℱ` be a finitely presented module on a scheme `X` which is finite locally free of constant
rank `r` on a scheme-theoretically dense open `U`, and let `b : X' ⟶ X` be the blowup of `X` in
the `r`-th Fitting ideal of `ℱ`. This file proves that `b^*ℱ` has projective dimension at most
one *affine-locally on `X'`*, together with the splitting that comes with it: around every point
of `X'` there is an affine open on which the sections of `b^*ℱ` are the direct sum of a finite
locally free module of rank `r` and a torsion module of projective dimension at most one.

This is the mathematical content of part (4) of Stacks tag 0ESN, whose proof there is the single
sentence "the statement on tor dimension follows from More on Algebra, Lemma 0F7M": two Fitting
ideals of `b^*ℱ` are computed, and the ring-level lemma 0F7M does the rest. The two ideals are
`Fit_r(b^*ℱ)`, which is the ideal sheaf of the exceptional divisor and so is principal on a
nonzerodivisor on suitable affine opens, and `Fit_{r-1}(b^*ℱ)`, which vanishes.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_sections_of_fittingIdeal_ideal_eq_span`
  transports Stacks 0F7M from a ring to an affine open of a scheme: if the `r`-th Fitting ideal
  sheaf of a finitely presented module is generated on an affine open by a nonzerodivisor and
  the `(r-1)`-st vanishes there, the sections have projective dimension at most one and split.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.fittingIdeal_pullback_blowUpToBase_eq_exceptionalIdeal`: the `r`-th Fitting
  ideal of `b^*ℱ` is the ideal sheaf of the exceptional divisor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ideal_fittingIdeal_pullback_pred_eq_bot`: the `(r-1)`-st Fitting ideal of
  `b^*ℱ` vanishes on every affine open.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_affineOpen_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_pullback_fittingBlowUp`:
  **the content of Stacks 0ESN (4).** Around every point of the blowup there is an affine open
  carrying the full conclusion of Stacks 0F7M for the sections of `b^*ℱ`.

## Implementation notes

The two Fitting-ideal computations are the only geometric input. `Fit_r(b^*ℱ)` is the inverse
image of `Fit_r(ℱ)` because Fitting ideal sheaves commute with base change (Stacks 0C3D,
`AlgebraicGeometry.fittingIdeal_comap`), and the inverse image of the centre of a blowup along
that blowup is by definition `AlgebraicGeometry.exceptionalIdeal`, which is an effective Cartier
divisor by Stacks 02OS (2) (`AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal`);
local principality on a nonzerodivisor is then the forward half of Stacks 01WS,
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`. The vanishing of
`Fit_{r-1}(b^*ℱ)` splits into the case `r = 0`, where the index is negative and the Fitting ideal
of any module vanishes, and the case where `Fit_{r-1}(ℱ)` already vanishes on `X` by scheme-
theoretic density of `U` (`AlgebraicGeometry.rank_eq_zero_or_fittingIdeal_pred_eq_bot`).

Only the `(r-1)`-st Fitting ideal is stated as vanishing *on an affine open* rather than as an
ideal sheaf: in the case `r = 0` the index is `-1`, where the ideal sheaf is not literally `⊥`
but its ideal on every affine open is, which is all that 0F7M consumes.

The conclusion is affine-local on `X'`. Globalizing it to perfectness of `b^*ℱ` and to a bound of
`1` on its Tor dimension, which is how Stacks 0ESN (4) reads, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPerfect_and_hasTorAmplitude_modulePullback_fittingBlowUp` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/Transform/FittingPerfectPullback.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ESN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ESN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F7M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F7M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C3D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C3D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Stacks 0F7M on an affine open -/

/-- **Stacks 0F7M on an affine open of a scheme.** Let `ℱ` be a finitely presented module on a
scheme `X` and let `V` be an affine open on which the `r`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of `ℱ` is
generated by a nonzerodivisor `g` and the `(r-1)`-st Fitting ideal sheaf vanishes. Then the
sections `Γ(V, ℱ)` have projective dimension at most one, their `g`-torsion is the `g`-power
torsion and also has projective dimension at most one, the quotient by it is finite locally free
of rank `r`, and `Γ(V, ℱ)` is the direct sum of the two.

This is the ring-level Stacks 0F7M,
`hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_and_split_of_fittingIdeal_eq_span_singleton`, read through the
identification of the Fitting ideal sheaf on an affine open with the Fitting ideal of the module
of sections (`AlgebraicGeometry.fittingIdeal_ideal`). -/
theorem hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_sections_of_fittingIdeal_ideal_eq_span
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) [F.IsFinitePresentation] (r : ℕ) (V : X.affineOpens)
    (g : Γ(X, V.1)) (hg : IsRegular g)
    (hspan : (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)).ideal V = Ideal.span {g})
    (hpred : (fittingIdeal F ((r : ℤ) - 1)).ideal V = ⊥) :
    let T := LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.lsmul Γ(X, V.1) Γ(F, V.1) g)
    let Q := Γ(F, V.1) ⧸ T
    HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of Γ(X, V.1) (ULift.{u} Γ(F, V.1))) 1 ∧
      T = Submodule.torsion' Γ(X, V.1) Γ(F, V.1) (Submonoid.powers g) ∧
      HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of Γ(X, V.1) (ULift.{u} T)) 1 ∧
      (∃ hfin : Module.Finite Γ(X, V.1) Q,
        letI := hfin
        ∃ hproj : Module.Projective Γ(X, V.1) Q,
          letI := hproj
          Module.rankAtStalk (R := Γ(X, V.1)) Q = fun _ => r) ∧
      Nonempty (Γ(F, V.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, V.1)] Q × T) := by
  have : F.IsFiniteType := SheafOfModules.instIsFiniteTypeOfIsFinitePresentation F
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := SheafOfModules.instIsQuasicoherentOfIsFinitePresentation F
  have hfinV : Module.Finite Γ(X, V.1) Γ(F, V.1) := moduleFinite_sections_on_affine F V.1 V.2
  have hfpV : Module.FinitePresentation Γ(X, V.1) Γ(F, V.1) :=
    finitePresentation_sections_on_affine F V
  have hspan' : _root_.fittingIdeal (R := Γ(X, V.1)) (M := Γ(F, V.1)) (r : ℤ) =
      Ideal.span {g} := by
    rw [← fittingIdeal_ideal F (r : ℤ) V]; exact hspan
  have hpred' : _root_.fittingIdeal (R := Γ(X, V.1)) (M := Γ(F, V.1)) ((r : ℤ) - 1) = ⊥ := by
    rw [← fittingIdeal_ideal F ((r : ℤ) - 1) V]; exact hpred
  exact hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_and_split_of_fittingIdeal_eq_span_singleton
    (R := Γ(X, V.1)) (M := Γ(F, V.1)) r g hg hspan' hpred'

/-! ### The two Fitting ideals of the pullback to the blowup -/

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)

/-- The pullback of a finitely presented module to the blowup in its `r`-th Fitting ideal is
finitely presented. -/
private theorem isFinitePresentation_pullback_blowUpToBase [F.IsFinitePresentation] (r : ℤ) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F r))).obj F).IsFinitePresentation :=
  @Stacks.SheafOfModules.modulePullback_isFinitePresentation _ _
    (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F r)).toLRSHom.toShHom F ‹_›

/-- The `r`-th Fitting ideal sheaf of the pullback of `ℱ` to the blowup of `X` in the `r`-th
Fitting ideal sheaf of `ℱ` is the ideal sheaf of the exceptional divisor.

Fitting ideal sheaves commute with base change (Stacks 0C3D) and the exceptional ideal sheaf is
by definition the inverse image of the centre. -/
theorem fittingIdeal_pullback_blowUpToBase_eq_exceptionalIdeal [F.IsFiniteType]
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] (r : ℕ) :
    fittingIdeal ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)))).obj F)
        (r : ℤ) =
      exceptionalIdeal (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)) :=
  (fittingIdeal_comap (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ))) F (r : ℤ)).symm

/-- The `(r-1)`-st Fitting ideal of the pullback of `ℱ` to the blowup of its `r`-th Fitting ideal
vanishes on every affine open, provided `ℱ` has rank `r` on a scheme-theoretically dense open.

For `r = 0` the index is negative, where the Fitting ideal of any finite module is zero. For
`r > 0` the `(r-1)`-st Fitting ideal already vanishes on `X`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.rank_eq_zero_or_fittingIdeal_pred_eq_bot`) and vanishing is inherited by the
inverse image. -/
theorem ideal_fittingIdeal_pullback_pred_eq_bot [F.IsFinitePresentation] (U : X.Opens) (r : ℕ)
    (hU : Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense U)
    (hrank : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj F) r)
    (V : (blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ))).affineOpens) :
    (fittingIdeal ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)))).obj F)
      ((r : ℤ) - 1)).ideal V = ⊥ := by
  have : F.IsFiniteType := SheafOfModules.instIsFiniteTypeOfIsFinitePresentation F
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := SheafOfModules.instIsQuasicoherentOfIsFinitePresentation F
  set b := blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)) with hb
  set G := (Scheme.Modules.pullback b).obj F with hG
  have hGfp : G.IsFinitePresentation := isFinitePresentation_pullback_blowUpToBase F r
  have hGft : G.IsFiniteType := SheafOfModules.instIsFiniteTypeOfIsFinitePresentation G
  have hGqc : G.IsQuasicoherent := SheafOfModules.instIsQuasicoherentOfIsFinitePresentation G
  have hfinV : Module.Finite Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V.1) Γ(G, V.1) :=
    moduleFinite_sections_on_affine G V.1 V.2
  rcases rank_eq_zero_or_fittingIdeal_pred_eq_bot F U r hU hrank with hr | hfit
  · -- `r = 0`: the index is `-1`, where every Fitting ideal vanishes.
    rw [fittingIdeal_ideal G ((r : ℤ) - 1) V]
    exact fittingIdeal_eq_bot_of_lt_zero (by omega : (r : ℤ) - 1 < 0)
  · -- `r > 0`: the `(r-1)`-st Fitting ideal vanishes on `X`, hence so does its inverse image.
    have hcomap : fittingIdeal G ((r : ℤ) - 1) = ⊥ := by
      rw [← fittingIdeal_comap b F ((r : ℤ) - 1), hfit, Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_bot]
    rw [hcomap]
    rfl

/-! ### Stacks 0ESN (4), affine-locally on the blowup -/

/-- **The content of Stacks 0ESN (4).** Let `ℱ` be a finitely presented module on a scheme `X`
which is finite locally free of constant rank `r` on a scheme-theoretically dense open `U`, and
let `b : X' ⟶ X` be the blowup of `X` in the `r`-th Fitting ideal of `ℱ`. Around every point of
`X'` there is an affine open `V` and a nonzerodivisor `g` generating the exceptional ideal on `V`
such that the sections `Γ(V, b^*ℱ)` have projective dimension at most one, their `g`-torsion is
the `g`-power torsion and also has projective dimension at most one, the quotient by it is finite
locally free of rank `r`, and `Γ(V, b^*ℱ)` is the direct sum of the two.

The `g`-torsion is the module of sections over `V` of the kernel of the canonical surjection from
`b^*ℱ` onto the strict transform, so this carries the projective-dimension bound of Stacks
0ESN (4) for both of the modules that part names. -/
theorem exists_affineOpen_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_pullback_fittingBlowUp
    [F.IsFinitePresentation] (U : X.Opens) (r : ℕ)
    (hU : Scheme.Opens.IsSchemeTheoreticallyDense U)
    (hrank : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u}
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj F) r)
    (y : blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ))) :
    ∃ (V : (blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ))).Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V), y ∈ V ∧
      ∃ g : Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V), IsRegular g ∧
        (exceptionalIdeal (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ))).ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = Ideal.span {g} ∧
        (let G := (Scheme.Modules.pullback
            (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)))).obj F
          let T := LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.lsmul
            Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V) Γ(G, V) g)
          let Q := Γ(G, V) ⧸ T
          HasProjectiveDimensionLE
              (ModuleCat.of Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V) (ULift.{u} Γ(G, V))) 1 ∧
            T = Submodule.torsion' Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V) Γ(G, V)
              (Submonoid.powers g) ∧
            HasProjectiveDimensionLE
              (ModuleCat.of Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V) (ULift.{u} T)) 1 ∧
            (∃ hfin : Module.Finite Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V) Q,
              letI := hfin
              ∃ hproj : Module.Projective Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V) Q,
                letI := hproj
                Module.rankAtStalk (R := Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V)) Q = fun _ => r) ∧
            Nonempty (Γ(G, V) ≃ₗ[Γ(blowUp (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)), V)] Q × T)) := by
  have : F.IsFiniteType := SheafOfModules.instIsFiniteTypeOfIsFinitePresentation F
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := SheafOfModules.instIsQuasicoherentOfIsFinitePresentation F
  have := isFinitePresentation_pullback_blowUpToBase F (r : ℤ)
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hyV, g, hg, hspan⟩ :=
    Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor
      (exceptionalIdeal (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ))) inferInstance y
  refine ⟨V, hV, hyV, g, hg, hspan, ?_⟩
  refine hasProjectiveDimensionLE_one_sections_of_fittingIdeal_ideal_eq_span
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (blowUpToBase (fittingIdeal F (r : ℤ)))).obj F) r ⟨V, hV⟩ g hg
    ?_ (ideal_fittingIdeal_pullback_pred_eq_bot F U r hU hrank ⟨V, hV⟩)
  rw [fittingIdeal_pullback_blowUpToBase_eq_exceptionalIdeal F r]
  exact hspan

/-! ### How the two conclusions of Stacks 0ESN (4) are globalized

Stacks 0ESN (4) reads: `b^*ℱ` and the kernel of its surjection onto the strict transform are
perfect `𝒪_{X'}`-modules of Tor dimension at most one. Both are global statements on `X'`, and
the projective resolution of length one proved above is the local data each of them consumes.

For `b^*ℱ` this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPerfect_and_hasTorAmplitude_modulePullback_fittingBlowUp`: the resolution
above makes the sections over an affine open the cokernel of an injection of finite projective
modules, which makes the restriction of `b^*ℱ` to that open perfect of Tor amplitude in
`[-1, 0]`, and both properties are local on the base
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isPerfect_and_hasTorAmplitude_of_forall_restrict`). For the kernel it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPerfect_strictTransformKernel_of_isFinitePresentation` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.hasTorAmplitude_strictTransformKernel_of_isFinitePresentation`, read off the
triangle of the kernel sequence in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/Transform/FittingPerfectTransform.lean`. -/

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
